  "id": "ideational-apraxia",
  "term": "ideational apraxia",
  "definition": "Ideational apraxia is a form of apraxia in which a person loses the ability to mentally plan the steps needed to carry out a learned action, even though the problem is not due to basic motor or sensory loss. It can show up as difficulty organizing familiar acts such as getting dressed.",
